        "calls": 1,
        "title": "CLI: Extract shared connection monitor singleton, pause probes during",
        "summary": "The adaptive health-check loop is extracted from the `useConnectionStatus` hook into a new process-wide singleton in `cli/src/utils/connection-monitor.ts`, owned by `createConnectionMonitor` with a lazily created instance accessible via `subscribeToConnectionStatus`. The hook now only subscribes to this shared state and reads its callback through a ref so that re-renders with unstable closure identity never reset the backoff timer or fire an extra probe. `use-chat-streaming.ts` calls `setConnectionMonitorBusy(isStreaming || isChainInProgress)` in an effect so the monitor pauses its 5s network probe during an active turn, because the turn's own success or failure is better evidence of connectivity than a concurrent probe. The interval escalation ladder (10s to 10min over 3 to 20 consecutive successes) and exponential failure backoff are preserved verbatim from the old hook.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "operators",
        "evidence": "The diff moves the adaptive health-check polling logic from `cli/src/hooks/use-connection-status.ts` into a new process-wide singleton in `cli/src/utils/connection-monitor.ts`, and adds `setConnectionMonitorBusy` called in `use-chat-streaming.ts` to pause probes during active streaming. The docstring in `connection-monitor.ts` states that the old hook-level loop reset backoff on every render, which flooded `/api/healthz` (1.17B GETs/week, ~74% of web Render service requests).",
        "userVisible": false,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "unknowns": "The diff does not show how the 1.17B GETs/week metric was collected or whether the reduction has been measured post-deploy; the docstring cites it as the historical root cause but no post-fix telemetry is included.",
