        "calls": 2,
        "title": "Connection monitor pauses polling when no subscribers remain",
        "summary": "The CLI connection monitor in `cli/src/utils/connection-monitor.ts` now pauses the health-check loop when the last listener unsubscribes, preventing the timer from continuing to poll the backend indefinitely. This addresses a bug where BYOK sessions that unsubscribed early would leave the monitor running forever. Additionally, an `inFlight` promise is introduced to deduplicate concurrent probes during rapid subscribe/unsubscribe cycles, ensuring that resubscribing adopts a pending check rather than starting a new one.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In `cli/src/utils/connection-monitor.ts`, the subscribe unsubscribe callback now checks `listeners.size === 0` to pause the loop, and a new `inFlight` variable deduplicates concurrent `checkConnection` calls during fast pause/resume cycles. The test file `cli/src/utils/__tests__/connection-monitor.test.ts` asserts that unsubscribing the last listener pauses the loop and that in-flight checks do not revive it.",
